11. Replace Old Tests and Add Regression Coverage

File: tests/systems/defense.test.mjs

Existing tests explicitly expect Shield Walking, including the 130-unit-per-second movement, gradual deceleration from running, carried jump momentum, and accelerated Shield waves.

These expectations must be removed or replaced.

Do not simply delete the tests and leave behavior untested.

Implement focused automated tests covering:

Test A — Shield while standing

Raise Shield while stationary.

Hold Left and Right separately for many simulation frames.

Verify that horizontal velocity and position do not change from voluntary movement.

Test B — Shield while running

Reach normal maximum running speed.

Raise Shield while still holding the running direction.

Verify the fighter immediately stops on the successful Shield activation step.

Verify it remains stationary for subsequent frames.

Test C — Both directions

Try Left, Right, opposite directional inputs and repeated directional changes while shielding.

Verify that none cause horizontal translation.

Verify permitted facing changes still work.

Test D — Shield release

Hold Shield and a direction.

Confirm the fighter is stationary.

Release Shield while continuing to hold that direction.

Verify movement resumes normally under existing acceleration rules.

Test E — Jump out of Shield

Raise Shield while holding Right.

Verify no walking.

Press Jump.

Verify the Shield drops and jumping works.

Verify no artificial Shield Walking momentum is inherited.

Verify ordinary airborne control remains available.

Test F — Blockstun

While Shield is raised, block an attack that causes blockstun.

Verify movement inputs do not produce walking during or after blockstun while the Shield remains raised.

Verify jumping remains restricted and buffered according to existing rules.

Test G — BlockPush

Use an attack with nonzero blockPush.

Verify a raised Shield still blocks the attack.

Verify the defender experiences the expected external displacement and its existing deceleration.

Verify held directional input does not add Shield Walking velocity.

Test H — Moving platforms

Place a shielding fighter on a moving platform.

Verify it is carried by the platform.

Verify it cannot walk relative to the platform while guarding.

Ensure the platform system is not broken.

Test I — All fighters

Verify stationary Shield behavior across every registered playable fighter with a valid ground Shield.

Include fighter #0006 and its ensemble rendering/physics behavior.

Do not hardcode different Shield speeds or behavior by fighter.

Test J — CPU controls

Verify CPU Shield actions do not cause walking.

Verify CPUs can release Shield, move, attack, and defend without deadlock.

Test K — Shield visuals

Verify the normal Shield outline and animation still render.

Verify the removed Shield Walking wave-speed feature is no longer present.

Check interior/rim synchronization and reduced-motion behavior.

Test L — Different input devices

Verify that keyboard, touch and gamepad inputs all produce the same stationary guarding behavior through the shared Fighter system.

Existing universal movement and control bindings must remain functional.

Test M — Frame-rate determinism

Verify that shielding behavior is consistent across Alva’s fixed-step simulation regardless of rendering frame rate.

