14. Acceptance Criteria

The implementation is complete only when all of these are true:

* Every valid ground Shield is stationary against voluntary horizontal movement.
* Raising Shield while running stops voluntary horizontal momentum immediately.
* Directional input cannot walk or creep while shielding.
* Movement resumes normally after Shield is lowered.
* Jumping out of Shield still works.
* Aerial Deflect remains unchanged.
* BlockPush and moving platforms still work.
* Perfect Shield, Energy costs, blockstun, defensive hit detection, and Shield animations remain functional.
* Shield Walking’s movement parameter, Fighter state, visual acceleration system, Discover entry and active localization have been removed.
* CPUs use the same stationary rules.
* The product specification and system documentation accurately describe stationary guarding.
* Tests cover the new behavior and the complete suite passes.

Important: Do not solve this by setting shieldWalkSpeed to zero. The goal is to remove Shield Walking as a mechanic entirely.

Keep the implementation minimal, clean, universal, and consistent with the existing architecture.

